      "created_at": "2025-01-11T20:09:34Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-01-11T20:09:34Z",
      "body": "Title like that would be fantastic, especially if the font size scales with size, or can be adjusted manually (latter is preferrable, but will probably break stuff if hard fixed when people resize via UI?).\r\nBorder settings would be nice to have too, and if we're talking re nice-to-haves - opacity setting / slider per item would be amazing for my personal style preference, but I can of course manage it personally via CSS on my side. At least having a custom CSS class option in 'Advanced options' maybe?\r\n\r\nRegarding the column collapse - I was thinking about something like Dashy handles it, see screenshots:\r\n![dash1](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/05b7d365-739a-432f-bab4-f97f6b5a1f2a)\r\n![dash2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a1c91f2-e5a3-49cc-ac2a-6cfd778f0d5d)\r\n\r\nI mean, it's already grid-based, so might as well? I tend to lean towards a 'cleaner' look personally, so if some sections aren't important to me, say, this week - I'd collapse them for a cleaner look\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
